# plans/plan_dx9.md D9-A5 scene corpus: sprite_sortmode_fronttoback_quad
# D9-93: the SpriteSortMode.FrontToBack counterpart of sprite_sortmode_deferred_quad.scene /
# sprite_sortmode_backtofront_quad.scene -- see the Deferred scene's own header comment for the
# full design rationale. This scene deliberately uses the OPPOSITE API insertion order from those
# two (GREEN depth=1.0 drawn FIRST, RED depth=0.0 drawn SECOND) specifically so FrontToBack's own
# ascending (near-to-far) reorder is genuinely discriminating: if FrontToBack correctly reorders
# to RED-then-GREEN (ascending by depth) before drawing, GREEN ends up on top again, producing
# the SAME final blend as sprite_sortmode_deferred_quad.scene (green-dominant) despite the
# REVERSED insertion order and a DIFFERENT sort mode -- proving the reorder actually happened. A
# broken/no-op FrontToBack (one that merely kept insertion order) would instead leave RED on top
# (red-dominant), distinguishably wrong.
width=256
height=256
profile=HiDef
clearcolor=0,0,0,255
spritebatchmode=true
texturewidth=1
textureheight=1
texturepixel=255,255,255,255
spritesortmode=FrontToBack
spritedraw=88,88,80,80,0,255,0,128,1.0
spritedraw=88,88,80,80,255,0,0,128,0.0
